    56	## §2. Defense Contract — the 5 dimensions
    57	
    58	Each S12 ticket (G.A-v2 onward) declares a `defense_contract` schema block.
    59	Schema is hierarchical so phases can declare only the fields they need; G.A-v2
    60	plugin validates presence + shape per ticket class.
    61	
    62	```yaml
    63	defense_contract:
    64	  # --- D1 Error detection ---
    65	  error_detection:
    66	    signal: prometheus_metric | structured_log | exit_code | endpoint_status | none
    67	    channel: <metric_name> | <log_query> | <endpoint_path> | null
    68	    detection_latency_p99: <duration>      # e.g., "30s"; null if signal=none
    69	    observability_test: <test_path>        # test exercising the failure path
    70	    alert_rule_id: <prometheus_rule_id> | null   # populated when AM rule exists
    71	
    72	  # --- D2 Exception handling ---
    73	  exception_handling:
    74	    enumerated_states: [<state_name>, ...]
    75	    remediation_hint_contract: <description> | none
    76	    user_facing: bool                      # if true, must include remediation in response
    77	    fail_loudly: bool                      # if true, must NOT silently swallow
    78	
    79	  # --- D3 Shutdown contract ---
    80	  shutdown_contract:
    81	    drain_seconds_p99: <int>               # null if feature has no lifecycle
    82	    cleanup_sequence: [<step>, ...]        # ordered
    83	    forced_termination_safe: bool          # is SIGKILL acceptable after grace?
    84	    state_persistence: <description> | none
    85	
    86	  # --- D4 Recovery path ---
    87	  recovery_path:
    88	    trigger_condition: <description>       # what indicates we're in failed state
    89	    steps: [<step>, ...]                   # ordered, idempotent
    90	    idempotent: bool                       # all steps idempotent (replay-safe)
    91	    rto_seconds_p99: <int>                 # recovery time objective
    92	    evidence_file: <path>                  # test / runbook proving it
    93	
    94	  # --- D5 Rescue path ---
    95	  rescue_path:
    96	    trigger_condition: <description>       # "recovery failed N times" / etc.
    97	    operator_actions: [<action>, ...]
    98	    authority_required: L1 | L2 | L3 | none   # per G.A-v0 + ADR-0033
    99	    audit_trail: <description>             # where rescue is logged
   100	```
